00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:29.260
<i>I was upset at the fact that Guin and Milady Kihel sent Sochie out to fight.</i>

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.850
<i>As a result, I didn't even care who this new enemy that appeared was.</i>

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:41.360
<i>However, I did come to understand just how powerful the White Doll is.</i>

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.960
<b>The Visit To a Grave</b>

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.760
l don't understand this...

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:04.850
Milady...

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:05.930
Milady, please...

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:07.770
I configured this device to recognize your voice.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.270
You simply need to ask for whatever item you wish to read up on.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.440
I don't even know what those things would be, so it's of no use to me.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.710
I'm not of the Moonrace.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.990
That has nothing to do with it...

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.950
I was saved by one of them.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.700
I never wanted that!

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.160
I'm sorry...

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.080
Don't apologize!

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.670
They won't simply give up and return to the moon easily, will they.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.330
Either they don't want to...

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.190
...or they're unable to.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:38.470
There are probably several different factors.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.330
Regardless...

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:49.270
Master Guin Rhineford, allow me to make a request.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.640
What is it?

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.070
l want to borrow Miss Kihel Heim from you.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.360
Borrow? That's a strange thing to ask...

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.150
...Ambassador Miran.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:08.540
Ahh, there you are, Loran! Sit it down to hide the White Doll beneath the tree line.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.830
It looks like something scraped it.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.250
Did the Militia's mechanics arrive here yet?

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.810
Thank you very much, Mr. Sid, Mr. Joseph.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.340
It's because of the sword of light in the shoulders...

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.760
...that we were able to make it out of there alive.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.050
Sword of light?

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:26.560
It's amazing. It cut right through the enemy's metallic baton.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.930
That's what Mr. Ladderum was saying.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:32.940
This manual mentions that it's called a "Beam Saber".

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.650
That thing's called a "computer notebook", correct?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.650
Do you know about it?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.070
Well, I am a scholar of the Dark History after all.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:47.030
We should make a copy of that unit's image and print it for the others. Then we'll make our way back to the excavation site.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.660
I've already asked Guin for more man power.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.960
There are differences in what's written on both sides.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.170
But you only use one side.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:59.750
Look, it's the same image on the other side, only reversed due to the projection.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:04.760
So the technology of the moon works like this, Loran?

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.850
Yeah, you could say that.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.470
What about it?

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:12.490
Nothing. We're lucky that the Militia has a person like you.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:17.570
This "Computer"... I want to see everything that's within it.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:20.930
Consider this the continuation of our party.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.570
After you.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:29.030
Welcome. Pardon me for calling you on such short notice.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.250
It's an honor to be invited here.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.040
I am Kihel Heim.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.460
I have arrived here, just as you requested.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.250
You're both so polite and obedient that it's almost unnerving for me.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.750
Please, make yourself comfortable.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.750
Yes, Queen Dianna.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.650
Yes, this is Sochie-

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.730
What's wrong, Jessica?

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.940
Lady Sochie, the Madame has been...

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.860
Mother? What's wrong?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.370
She's keeps going on and on about how lonely she feels... I feel the same way.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.660
Lady Sochie...

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:13.910
Please get Lady Kihel and return and visit us at once!

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.530
Is your mother not doing well?

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.040
Well, Jessica asked me to visit and cheer them up.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.840
I see.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.550
I wonder if Sam has built a good tomb stone for my father yet...

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.640
I'm terribly embarrassed.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.350
From the looks of it, none of my orders reached the forces who arrived on Earth ahead of me.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.430
With all of your military's advanced technology...

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.350
...I can't believe there'd be so much miscommunication over orders.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:42.230
The sights of Earth's marvelous beauty overwhelmed many of us.

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:46.350
A lack of proper communications only contributed to that trance like state.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.950
As long as you personally have peaceful intentions...

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.450
I believe that the current situation can still be changed.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.660
You can expect no less from us, Master Guin Rhineford.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.290
Why would you have an airship land at this castle?

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.170
l am using it to investigate the damaged caused by the fighting.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.750
And for the sake of helping the victims.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.050
I see.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.720
Will it be flying soon?

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:08.970
Queen Dianna?

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:12.140
It, in fact, will be. Would you like to accompany us on the observations?

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:16.180
The view from the airship is a beautiful and breath-taking sight to behold.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.560
Beautiful and breath-taking scenery.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.560
I've not yet had the chance to survey such beauty.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:23.610
Nor the damage from this war.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:24.940
I don't like it.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.940
Surveying the damage is necessary...

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:31.570
And I have always wanted to fly in an airship.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:34.870
In that case, I'll prepare the ship for your welcome.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.370
That is, if you would find it permissible, Sir Miran.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.750
I prefer it if you'd allow our forces to escort the ship.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.460
If that is what you wish.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.250
Miss Kihel, as I prepare things...

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.960
...please stay here with Dianna.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:47.880
Of course.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.550
Then I will have Lieutenant Harry prepare to lead the guard.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.140
Very well.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:56.840
In the meantime, why don't we converse over a cup of tea?

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.320
Are you left handed?

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:15.150
No. I am like a mirror before you.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:22.030
My My, Queen Dianna.

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:35.550
The two of us look exactly the same.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:38.970
I must admit, I'd noticed the exact same thing.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.230
Have the Kapool dig the left leg out from there.

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:51.270
Those working on the right, help those on the left.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.860
Here's the cash we promised.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.570
It should be enough for you to buy the building.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.830
Thank you, Sir.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.460
I never expected your discovery to be so impressive.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:10.840
That's right, it is pretty large.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.970
Will you help us operate this?

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.130
What?

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.930
No. I want to use this money to expand my bakery.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:22.430
Indeed. I guess I'll order the plane mechanics to inspect and learn to operate it.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:24.560
I suppose so.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.560
Still, you'll be fine.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.150
It should have a manual with it.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:30.940
Loran... Fran...

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:34.270
I'm going to become a great baker!

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:38.530
I've always wanted to wear a dress like this.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.950
What do you think?

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.540
I'm not quite sure how you'd feel about it, but since we'll be riding the airship soon...

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.330
It may be better to dress casually.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.540
Really...

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.250
Well, then these designs may be a bit simpler.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.040
But what color would be more suitable?

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.260
Hmm... well, Miss Kihel...

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.550
...can I have you model this for me?

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.050
You mean me?

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:02.930
What do you think?

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.360
Miss Kihel...

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:11.230
Could I have you try on my outfit as well?

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:13.440
You want me to wear your gown, Queen Dianna?

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.450
That's right, please do.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.060
Sure.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.360
That's the last piece.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:23.240
Could you please turn around for me?

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:25.960
I see...

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.960
...so that's what I look like from behind.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.550
You HAVE seen yourself in pictures, right?

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:36.760
But that's not quite like seeing the real thing.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.340
I'm relieved to finally see it for myself.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:46.400
Miran, let us continue surveying the sights. Please accompany me.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:49.140
That was great,  Miss Kihel.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:53.190
Queen Dianna...She must have been very lonely.

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:54.740
What is it?

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.950
It's Ambassador Miran. I'm here to pick up Her Majesty.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:59.070
You may enter.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.370
Queen Dianna?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.370
From this point on...

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.700
...Kihel will be Dianna Soriel....

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.120
And I will be Kihel Heim.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.040
What should we do if someone discovers the truth?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.090
If that happens, then we'll apologize to them for it.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:15.250
Queen Dianna, Ambassador Miran is here.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.470
My my, Queen Dianna...

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:31.860
Dianna Counter's mechanical dolls will escort the ship for us.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.900
Issue the command that nobody is to fire upon them.

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:37.650
Will it be okay to fly to Vicinity?

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:40.660
That route won't have anything more than a few wrecked long ranged artillery remnants.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.240
Mr. Guin, someone is here to see you.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.160
Who is it?

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.370
Loran Cehack and Sochie Heim.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.660
Laura and the lady, you say?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.210
Allow them in.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.040
Half of the castle is to be made serviceable for the Queen.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.170
Are our arrangements proceeding as planned?

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.050
So, what is it?

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:58.260
This is Mr. Sid's report, and also...

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.760
And also, About my sister...

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.550
...she doesn't have time to be hanging around the Moonrace.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:05.560
I'm here to inform her that mother's health is deteriorating and request that we both return to Vicinity.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.560
"Beam Saber", is it?

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.560
You used a thing like that to cut into the enemy's mechanical dolls?

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:15.070
While you may want to see it as a sword of light, it actually uses highly condensed super-heated particles.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.530
Lord Guin Rhineford!

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.360
The Airship is already prepared.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.950
You can ride it to Vicinity.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:23.070
Soldier, show them onto the Airship.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.160
Sir.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.240
Metallic particles, even?

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.070
Thank you very much, Sir.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.960
Your sister and I will follow soon.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:32.960
Yes.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.670
Aren't you glad we came?

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.500
Try not to look below you.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:07.960
After you.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:12.160
Miss Kihel, Go ahead.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.280
I board with gratitude.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.770
So, is this the gondola?

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:42.070
This is also my first time standing inside this thing.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:45.280
Be careful how you speak. Remember, you are Dianna Soriel.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.620
You have to carry yourself with grace.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:51.580
With grace, huh? You mean I need to use a more authoritative tone?

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.830
I'm not sure if I can do it.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.000
Please do not worry.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:01.490
This airship is well suspended in the air.

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:03.090
I follow you.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:06.590
Queen Dianna, I think there's a seat in the back back meant for overseeing the view.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.170
Shall we take it, then?

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:13.170
- Dianna?
- Sister?

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.600
Loran? Sochie?

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:16.560
Sochie Heim?

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.110
I'm very sorry, I was not aware that...

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:22.280
Her Majesty, Dianna Soriel would be here on the airship.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.490
How do you do. It looks like you already know my name.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.990
Your sister spoke of you to me.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.780
Mr. Loran, please make yourself at ease.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.660
Thank you, your Majesty.

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:38.080
Sister, Mother was crying because she's been feeling extremely lonely.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.000
Mr. Guin said that this airship...

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:43.090
...would by flying around Vicinity, and then returning here.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.010
Perhaps we could stop there for a while.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:49.890
Yes, l would like to do that as well.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:52.930
If that would be permissible, Sir Guin Rhineford.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:54.680
If you wish.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.390
Miss Kihel, please prepare a pot of tea for us.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:58.600
Of course.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:02.740
I'll do it. The tea set's right over here.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:06.390
You idiot. That's my sister's job.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.280
We'll head out as well.

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.640
It's so beautiful.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.810
Yes. Today's view is magnificent.

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.600
As Sir Guin has said...

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.400
...we should not allow this war to ruin this scenery.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.780
Yes. The flames of war cannot be allowed to destroy this.

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:45.820
Miss Kihel...

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:48.400
Haven't you seen these sights before?

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.780
Yes, of course I have.

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:56.200
Don't you mean to say that the view on earth changes day by day, Kihel?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.370
A different view every day.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.370
The landscape on the moon is always the same.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.920
It won't endure any noticeable changes after even an entire century passes, Queen Dianna?

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:05.590
Y... Yes, that's correct.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:07.590
There is never any change.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:11.170
However, the view here on earth is awe inspiring.

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:18.270
That one's a SUMO Mobile Suit from the Royal Guard, right?

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:19.980
The Dianna Counter's...

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:23.650
...mechanical dolls are usually called Mobile Suits.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.570
"Suits" are strange things.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:30.700
A biplane has a far more elegant appearance to it, does it not, Queen Dianna?

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:33.990
It truly is a vehicle design one could only see here on the earth.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:36.200
Two pairs of wings is a beautiful sight.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:37.870
What's that?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.410
It was caused by a bomb.

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:43.790
Nocis city was also badly damaged.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:45.790
It looks like it was burned.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:48.000
It does nothing but destroy such beauty...

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.380
...and cause food shortages for those who live there.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:51.590
Honestly...

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.390
- Miss Kihel...
- Yes?

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:55.800
Sir Miran, Queen Dianna...

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:57.350
I would like to borrow Lady Kihel.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.470
As you wish.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.730
- Follow me to the cabin.
- Right.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.400
Do you have any extra clothing with you?

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:06.400
I'm sorry, I don't.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.890
How about you, Sochie?

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:10.780
What do you mean?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:13.070
Queen Dianna is dressed rather oddly.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.070
I would like her to wear something a bit more normal...

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.370
...in order to avoid being targeted by the Militia's solders.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.790
My sister's room survived the fire, so we could visit there when we get home.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.580
Why couldn't she just use some of her items?

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:23.870
Wouldn't that work?

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:26.000
Well, I was hoping...

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.790
I could find some clothes on this ship that would work.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.800
You idiot, there wouldn't be any around here!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.880
There is nothing to be done until we land, then.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.680
If we do go to your home, may I borrow your clothing, Kihel?

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:39.310
You both seem to have the same body shape, so I wonder if she'll fit them?

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:41.930
They would fit her as though they were tailor made.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:43.890
Why are you so excited?

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:46.400
She's the leader of our enemy.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.900
Are you glad to lend your clothing to such a person?

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:52.690
Our father died because that woman decided to come to Earth!

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:57.870
They're the reason that our mother has lost her senses!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.290
Why should we help protect someone like her!?

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.570
Please understand, Milady Sochie.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.000
But... I'm right, aren't I?

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.460
Yes, you are right, Milady Sochie.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.010
You must understand.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.380
I'll make sure that it works out.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:19.170
Until then, I'm asking you for this, Sochie Heim.

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:28.100
Harry, I hope this all works out.

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:31.110
l cannot agree.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:35.200
Vicinity hosts a large number of the Militia's currently active guerrilla factions.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.570
What if something were to happen?

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:40.580
That's what you said...

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.500
...before we came down to earth, Ambassador Miran.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.780
However...

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.580
If anything bad were to happen to you...

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:53.590
Regardless of the friends or enemies we may encounter...

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:57.000
We must see how their citizens live for ourselves.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:09.980
- Now, Pull!
- One, two, Pull!

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:19.980
Our path has to be kept a secret, understood?

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.990
Her Majesty Dianna is in the second truck.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:25.290
Watch it closely.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:28.220
The Militia army is always active in this area.

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:31.080
- Shall we go?
- Please

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:36.000
- Follow the car ahead of us.
- Right.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:04.080
Was the tunnel where the White Doll's hammer was uncovered buried beneath this rubble?

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:09.070
No. Now, the entire area has been destroyed...

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:13.990
The war has even spread to a remote village like this one...

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:23.050
Lady Kihel! Lady Sochie!

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:26.680
You finally made it back! It's been so long and you've been so busy...

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:29.060
Lord Guin, Your Majesty!

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:32.690
Thank you so much for bringing the ladies back to us.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.690
It's no problem, Jessica.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:36.570
I thank you.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:41.190
Lady Kihel, your mother has been waiting to see you.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:48.080
If you'd like to step inside...

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.370
...I'm sure they'd be willing to let you in.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:52.050
Would that be alright?

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:54.000
If Queen Dianna Soriel has come to see the people...

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.790
l don't see a problem with you doing so.

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:00.380
Laura, lead me in.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:01.380
Yes.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:05.390
Sorry for interrupting, it's Queen Dianna Soriel.

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:06.850
Please come in.

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:12.190
This summer holiday's been a long one, hasn't it?

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:13.270
Yes it has.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:15.270
There's been too much homework, so l couldn't make it back before this.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:17.110
It's fine, Sochie.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.780
I am just happy to see your face again.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.490
Right, Jessica?

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:25.700
Ma'am, Lady Kihel has returned as well.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.400
Mother.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:31.320
Is everything going well at your University?

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:35.000
Of course. I've made several friends there.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.380
I'm sorry to have called you all the way back here.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.080
No.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:41.000
Mother...

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:45.390
In this big house, Sam and Jessica are all I have left.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:48.680
Your father left for the mountains to try and improve productivity in the mines.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:51.390
For the sake of our leader...

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:54.800
The war I've instigated is against people like this...?

00:20:57.250 --> 00:21:00.400
Your hands are warm, Kihel.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.990
Thank you very much, mother.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:06.780
Sister, it's time for us to go say hello to our father.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:09.280
Sure.

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:13.790
Tell your father not to worry himself over us.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.070
Yes.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:36.940
Lady Kihel?

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:39.270
Oh father, I'm so very sorry!

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:42.780
I'm sorry it took so long for me to come back...

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:46.780
It's just that I have been kept so very busy by my work.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:51.690
I really am terribly sorry, father. Please understand this and be at peace...

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:54.900
L- Lady Kihel...

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:57.780
Dianna Soriel...

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:00.990
Thank you so much.

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:07.000
That...That really did come from deep within your heart, didn't it?

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:41.980
<i>As mechanical dolls continue to...</i>

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:43.400
<i>...be excavated from the Mountain Cycle...</i>

00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:46.070
<i>The Militia army battles against the Soleil.</i>

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:49.780
<i>During the attack, the Soleil launches to retreat.</i>

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:53.320
<i>While she's on the ship, Milady Kihel suggests that the negotiations continue...</i>

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:54.570
<i>However...</i>

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:58.190
<i>The Mountain Cycle ends up being attacked as well.</i>

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.460
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN-A GUNDAM...

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:03.430
<i>The Destruction of Nocis</i>

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:09.790
<b>The Destruction of Nocis</b>

00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:05.720
"The winds of negotiation will become still."
